From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:07:45 -0500
Subject: feat: bring Arc's splits and archived tabs across

A split view of Arc's came in as nothing: the importer did not know the kind, so
its tabs went with it. Its archive stayed in Arc.

A split's panes are now tabs in its place, each knowing its split, so whatever
takes tabs takes them: the pinned run, the tabs under the line, a folder. Once
they are where they belong the first two make one split, side by side, half and
half. Chromium's split holds two, so of three or four panes the others are tabs
after it, and a split with one pane left is that tab. Favorites take no split.
Both panes load when the row is opened.

Arc's archive, StorableArchiveItems.json beside the sidebar, is read from a copy
on the pool. Its items, closed by Arc's timer or by the person, become rows of
the archive with a reason of "import", shown as "archived in Arc", under Arc's
date, in the Space their Arc Space became. They come with the Other tabs box, a
page once a Space. The row is a record the list of closed tabs holds, so it
restores, searches and survives a restart as any close does. They go behind what
the list holds and only as far as it has room, through a new
TabRestoreService::AddClosedTabs, so a close of the person's own is never pushed
out; the import waits for the list to load first. What has no room is counted, and
comes at a later import. A row an import brought does not come again.

The archive keeps such a row from the import, not from Arc's date: by Arc's date
most of an old archive would come in out of sight.

The folder an archived tab was in is not read, and neither is a split's layout:
no public description says how they are written. Both shapes are as public
exporters read them; no real file has been seen. The tests use made-up files.
The page after an import no longer says these do not come across, and names what
does not: a split of more than two.

FromArcPageTest.ANewImportReadsThePageAgain raced the reload it waits for, and no
longer fails when the page has no frame to answer with.

Why: people leaving Arc keep what they kept there (BACKLOG S-103, import I7,
archive A8, A11).

Removable when: Arc's files are gone from people's computers. AddClosedTabs goes
with them.
